+### Button group classes
+
+The button group key ships whole, in its own partial after the vertical rule in the components
+layer: the horizontal group, the vertical group, the relationships that join their children, and
+the sized group families. It declares no custom property of its own. Its radius reads
+`--bs-border-radius` and its overlap reads `--bs-border-width`, and `_tokens.scss` already declares
+each of those over `--vn-radius-base` and `--vn-border-width`, so a consumer retuning either name
+moves the group.
+
+A group lays its children out as an inline flex line, and each child grows and shrinks from an
+automatic basis, so the children share the group's free space. The vertical group turns that line
+into a column, aligns it to the leading edge, and stretches every child to the group's own width.
+
+Neighbouring children overlap rather than doubling their shared border: each child after the first
+is pulled back by one border width, on the inline axis in a horizontal group and on the block axis
+in a vertical one. A child the reader is addressing lifts over that shared border, and the states
+that lift it are a checked or focused `.btn-check` input's label, a hovered child, a focused child,
+a pressed child, and a child carrying `.active`.
+
+The corners follow the same physical reading. A horizontal group clears the trailing corners of
+every child but the last and the leading corners of every child but the first, so the group keeps
+one rounded outline; a vertical group clears the bottom corners and the top corners the same way. A
+group nested inside a group is treated as one of those children, and its own children carry the
+corners it would have carried. A child carrying `.dropdown-toggle` keeps its trailing corners,
+which is what leaves room for the split toggle Disclosure ships.
+
+The `.btn-group-sm > .btn` and `.btn-group-lg > .btn` twins ship from
+`src/styles/components/_button.scss`, where Bootstrap's own `@extend` puts them, so the sized group
+families resolve the Button size each name declares and this partial writes nothing for them.
+
+`tests/src/styles/components/button-group.test.ts` reads each resolved treatment in the browser: the
+direction and child growth, the overlap measured as the offset between neighbours, every corner of
+every child position, each lift driven or written, the retuned compatibility variables, and the
+published radius and density factors.
+
+These are the key's recorded departures.
+
